interface.longDescription:
Fleek is a subscription distribution platform for businesses. Card programmes, loyalty and rewards platforms, employee-benefits and gifting platforms, and telcos use Fleek to offer streaming, music, AI, sports and other subscription brands to their users through an API, a white-label storefront or bulk codes.

This plugin answers one question inside ChatGPT: which subscription brands could my programme offer its users in a given market? It can:
- search Fleek's catalogue by market, region or category (for example streaming in the GCC or music in the UK);
- look up one brand: its category, the markets it is available in and how partners can deliver it;
- shortlist 3 to 6 brands for a card, loyalty, employee-benefits or telco programme in a market, each with a one-line reason;
- give the link for a business to open its own Fleek partner workspace;
- explain to a business that sells a subscription how to get it carried by these programmes, with the merchant sign-up link;
- explain to a creator (an influencer, a community or a cashback app) how to open a Fleek shop for their audience, with the creator sign-up link.

Who it is for: people who design or run rewards, benefits and bundle programmes at businesses.

Limitations: it is read-only and needs no account. It does not sell anything, place orders or process payments, and it cannot see or change a Fleek workspace. It covers the brands and markets in Fleek's catalogue; a brand it doesn't list may still be available on request from the Fleek team.
